#{\footnote # drawing}${\footnote $ Drawing}K{\footnote K Drawing}+{\footnote + procedures:010}
\pard\sb120\sa120\li120{\b\fs28 Drawing}\par
\pard\li120\sa60\sb60{\b To draw}\par
\pard\li360\fi-240\sa60 1.\tab Choose a tool from the toolbox at the left.\par
2.\tab Choose the line width below the toolbox.\par
3.\tab Click a colour in the palette with the left button for the foreground, the right button for the background.\par
4.\tab Drag in the picture.\par
\pard\li120\sa120 The eraser paints with the background colour; the paint roller fills an area with the foreground colour.\par
\page
#{\footnote # saving_pictures}${\footnote $ Saving Pictures}K{\footnote K Saving Pictures}+{\footnote + procedures:020}
\pard\sb120\sa120\li120{\b\fs28 Saving Pictures}\par
\pard\li120\sa120 Save keeps the picture as a bitmap file (.BMP) that Paintbrush, Write and other programs can open.\par
\page
